  "title": "Gusto Alternatives Compared by Published Payroll Price",
  "h1": "Gusto Alternatives Compared by Published Payroll Price",
  "metaDescription": "Gusto alternatives compared: OnPay, Patriot Software, Square Payroll, Justworks, Paychex Flex and ADP RUN, with base fees and per-person prices.",
  "published": "2026-11-22",
  "updated": "2026-11-22",
  "intro": "OnPay, Patriot Software and Square Payroll are three Gusto alternatives with published per-person payroll prices, and Justworks adds a professional employer organization (PEO) route. Paychex Flex and ADP RUN publish no price and quote on request. The right pick depends on whether a business wants a lower base fee, a point-of-sale tie-in, bundled human resources (HR) tools or a quote-based provider with phone support.\n\n[Gusto](https://www.gusto.com/product/pricing) prices payroll as a monthly base fee plus a fee for each person paid. Simple costs $49 a month plus $6 per person, Plus costs $80 plus $12, and Premium costs $180 plus $22. Gusto lists no contracts and free account setup, and says a business can switch or cancel anytime.\n\nThe worked examples on this page use a 10-person team, so both the base fee and the per-person fee show up in each total. Tax, add-ons and promotions are left out of that arithmetic.\n\nPayroll usually sits next to a bookkeeping or accounting tool. For those, see the [best bookkeeping services for small businesses](/roundup/best-bookkeeping-services-for-small-businesses/) roundup, the [best accounting software for freelancers](/roundup/best-accounting-software-for-freelancers/) list, and the [QuickBooks alternatives](/alternatives/quickbooks/), [FreshBooks alternatives](/alternatives/freshbooks/) and [Wave alternatives](/alternatives/wave/) guides. The [comparison hub](/compare/) collects more software breakdowns.",
  "tableTitle": "Gusto Alternatives: Published Payroll Prices Compared",
  "tableNote": "Fees and prices from each provider's own website, checked November 22, 2026. Regular monthly list prices in US dollars; promotions, tax and optional add-ons are excluded unless named in the row.",
